## Available routes

- [/stack/audit](/stack/audit)

| name | kind | required | description |
|---|---|---|---|
| fix | bool | no | Repair what the audit finds. |
- [/stack/deploy](/stack/deploy)
  - **description:** Stands in for a deploy command.

| name | kind | required | description |
|---|---|---|---|
| dry-run | bool | no | Plan without applying. |
| elevated | bool | no | Deploy as an administrator. |
- [/stack/serve](/stack/serve)
  - **description:** Stands in for a command.

from **VerboseLogger**

| name | kind | required | description |
|---|---|---|---|
| verbose | bool | no | Log every request. |

## Inherited params

Taken by every route above, read by the middleware or server declaring them.

from **HelpHandler**

| name | kind | required | description |
|---|---|---|---|
| help | bool | no | List the routes beneath this one and the params each takes, rather than calling it. |

from **PageClasses**

| name | kind | required | description |
|---|---|---|---|
| color-scheme | one of: light, dark | no | Pin the page's color scheme over the negotiated one. |

from **CliServer**

| name | kind | required | description |
|---|---|---|---|
| accept | alloc::vec::Vec<alloc::string::String> | no | The media types to answer in, highest priority first, eg `--accept=text/html,text/plain`. Defaults to ANSI for a terminal and markdown when stdout is not one. |
| server | server names, comma separated, eg "http,ssh" | no | Which declared servers boot, comma separated, eg `http,ssh`. |
